From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 18:14:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kdesktop: put the lock control FIFOs in the per-user socket
 directory

kdesktop_lock creates two control FIFOs and has been unable to create
either of them for any ordinary user. They were placed in
/tmp/tdesocket-global, which tdm creates as root before anyone logs in, so
mknod() failed with EACCES on every lock attempt. On one desktop this
produced 83 identical warnings in a single session, and the message it
prints is the only sign of it: neither mknod() nor mkdir() had its return
value read, so the failure surfaced indirectly and looked like a warning
about an optional feature rather than a feature that had never once
worked.

The directory creation could not have helped even without the ownership
problem. mkdir(FIFO_DIR, 0644) asks for a directory with no execute bit,
which cannot be entered to create anything inside it.

A shared directory is the wrong home regardless. The inbound FIFO accepts
commands that dismiss the unlock dialog and display arbitrary text, and
the outbound one carries the PIN the user has typed. Making the shared
directory writable so that every user could create their own nodes would
let any local user pre-create another user's control socket, drive their
lock screen and read their PIN. That is a worse fault than the one being
fixed.

Resolve the location from TDEGlobal::dirs() instead. The socket resource
is per-user and per-host and tdelibs creates it mode 0700, which is what
these FIFOs need; both are created 0600 rather than the inbound one being
world-readable. A privileged helper running as root reaches them exactly
as before, and a module running as another user no longer can.

Report a failing mknod() with its errno and treat an existing FIFO as the
success it is, chmod()ing only what was actually created.

Drop the umask handling rather than repair it. The original set umask(0)
process-wide and never restored it, and this runs in a worker thread, so
any file the rest of the process created in that window got whatever mode
it asked for. It was never needed: a umask can only clear bits, 0600 has
none a sane one would clear, and the chmod sets the mode outright.

Signed-off-by: Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>
---
 kdesktop/lock/lockprocess.cpp | 62 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 kdesktop/lock/lockprocess.h   |  9 +++--
 2 files changed, 58 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kdesktop/lock/lockprocess.cpp b/kdesktop/lock/lockprocess.cpp
index e0eeed05d..24fbd4365 100644
--- a/kdesktop/lock/lockprocess.cpp
+++ b/kdesktop/lock/lockprocess.cpp
@@ -78,6 +78,7 @@
 #include <sys/resource.h>
 #endif
 #include <stdio.h>
+#include <string.h>
 #include <sys/stat.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <errno.h>
@@ -2997,24 +2998,65 @@ void ControlPipeHandlerObject::run(void) {
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * These FIFOs are privileged. The inbound one accepts commands that
+	 * dismiss the unlock dialog and display arbitrary text, and the
+	 * outbound one carries the PIN the user has typed. They therefore
+	 * belong in the per-user socket directory, which tdelibs creates mode
+	 * 0700, and not in a directory shared with every other user of the
+	 * machine.
+	 *
+	 * The shared /tmp/tdesocket-global was unusable in practice as well as
+	 * unsafe: tdm creates it as root before any user logs in, so mknod()
+	 * here failed with EACCES on every lock for an ordinary user.
+	 */
+	TQString socket_dir = TDEGlobal::dirs()->saveLocation("socket");
+	if (socket_dir.isEmpty()) {
+		printf("[kdesktop_lock] Warning: no per-user socket directory available. Interactive logon modules may not function properly.\n");
+		mRunning = false;
+		TQApplication::eventLoop()->exit(-1);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	char fifo_file[PATH_MAX];
 	char fifo_file_out[PATH_MAX];
-	snprintf(fifo_file, PATH_MAX, FIFO_FILE, display_number);
-	snprintf(fifo_file_out, PATH_MAX, FIFO_FILE_OUT, display_number);
-
-	/* Create the FIFOs if they do not exist */
-	umask(0);
-	mkdir(FIFO_DIR,0644);
-	mknod(fifo_file, S_IFIFO|0644, 0);
-	chmod(fifo_file, 0644);
+	snprintf(fifo_file, PATH_MAX, "%s/" FIFO_FILE_NAME,
+		 socket_dir.local8Bit().data(), display_number);
+	snprintf(fifo_file_out, PATH_MAX, "%s/" FIFO_FILE_OUT_NAME,
+		 socket_dir.local8Bit().data(), display_number);
+
+	/*
+	 * Create the FIFOs if they do not exist. An existing FIFO is not an
+	 * error; any other failure is, and is reported here rather than left
+	 * to surface as an unexplained absence later.
+	 *
+	 * No umask juggling. The original set umask(0) process-wide and never
+	 * restored it, and this runs in a worker thread, so any file the rest
+	 * of the process created meanwhile got whatever mode it asked for. It
+	 * was never needed either: a umask can only clear bits, 0600 has none
+	 * that a sane one would clear, and the chmod below sets the mode
+	 * outright regardless of umask.
+	 */
+	if (mknod(fifo_file, S_IFIFO|0600, 0) != 0 && errno != EEXIST) {
+		printf("[kdesktop_lock] Warning: cannot create control socket '%s': %s. Interactive logon modules may not function properly.\n",
+		       fifo_file, strerror(errno));
+	}
+	else {
+		chmod(fifo_file, 0600);
+	}
 
 	mParent->mPipe_fd = open(fifo_file, O_RDONLY | O_NONBLOCK);
 	if (mParent->mPipe_fd > -1) {
 		mParent->mPipeOpen = true;
 	}
 
-	mknod(fifo_file_out, S_IFIFO|0600, 0);
-	chmod(fifo_file_out, 0600);
+	if (mknod(fifo_file_out, S_IFIFO|0600, 0) != 0 && errno != EEXIST) {
+		printf("[kdesktop_lock] Warning: cannot create control socket '%s': %s. Interactive logon modules may not function properly.\n",
+		       fifo_file_out, strerror(errno));
+	}
+	else {
+		chmod(fifo_file_out, 0600);
+	}
 
 	mParent->mPipe_fd_out = open(fifo_file_out, O_RDWR | O_NONBLOCK);
 	if (mParent->mPipe_fd_out > -1) {
diff --git a/kdesktop/lock/lockprocess.h b/kdesktop/lock/lockprocess.h
index b0e33aad2..e81498c6a 100644
--- a/kdesktop/lock/lockprocess.h
+++ b/kdesktop/lock/lockprocess.h
@@ -40,9 +40,12 @@ struct GreeterPluginHandle {
 	kgreeterplugin_info *info;
 };
 
-#define FIFO_DIR "/tmp/tdesocket-global"
-#define FIFO_FILE "/tmp/tdesocket-global/kdesktoplockcontrol-%d"
-#define FIFO_FILE_OUT "/tmp/tdesocket-global/kdesktoplockcontrol_out-%d"
+/*
+ * Names only. The directory is the per-user socket location resolved at
+ * runtime from TDEGlobal::dirs(); see ControlPipeHandlerObject::run().
+ */
+#define FIFO_FILE_NAME "kdesktoplockcontrol-%d"
+#define FIFO_FILE_OUT_NAME "kdesktoplockcontrol_out-%d"
 
 typedef TQValueList<Window> TQXLibWindowList;
 
